RX, VCC pin3->+5V with C31 100n, VIO pin5->+3.3V with C32 100n, S pin8->GND normal mode, GND pin2->GND, CANH pin7->CAN2+, CANL pin6->CAN2-); no CANH/CANL swap found under y-mirror transform.\",\"Verified NUP2105L dual ESD clamp (D10/D11) cathodes to CAN2+ and CAN2-, anode pin3 to GND; verified 47p filter caps C29/C30 from CAN2+/CAN2- to GND in both sheet instances.\",\"Checked internal dual-wideband CAN2 termination: sheet resistor R36 (120R, 1206) is dnp/in_bom-no with 'n.p.' annotation; confirmed on saved board that both instance refs R36 and R37 bridge /CAN2+ to /CAN2- and appear in geometry dnp_refs.\",\"Cross-checked board geometry pad nets for U21 (TJA1051T-3: /CAN_TX2, /CAN_RX2, /CAN2+, /CAN2-, +5V, +3.3V, GND) and U1 (f042_wideband_module: /CAN_RX, /CAN_TX, /LSU_* pins) within the included geometry prefix.\",\"Reviewed DRC execution record (kicad-cli 10.0.7, exit 0, severity-all with schematic parity), console log counts (142 violations, 0 unconnected, 114 parity issues), and the included prefix of work/drc/drc.json (parity warnings, silk_over_copper, lib_footprint_mismatch/issues, extra_footprint list).\",\"Correlated the 15 extra_footprint parity items (U10 MAX9924, R25-R34, C23-C25, JP1) with the missing 'VR Conditioner.kicad_sch' sheet file that caused ERC and netlist checks to be malformed.\",\"Confirmed DRC reports zero unconnected items on the saved board (fill state as saved).\",\"Sanity-checked README feature claims against visible board content (dual CAN transceivers, dual wideband module footprints, VNL5090 lowside drivers, TLE9201SG H-bridge, DRV8825 stepper header).\"],\"limitations\":[\"work/drc/drc.json supplied only as a 100000-byte prefix: the 13 error-severity violations (padstack, annular_width, starved_thermal per the check's by_type summary) are not individually visible, so affected refs/locations could not be verified.\",\"work/geometry/geometry.json supplied only as a 100000-byte prefix: the second wideband module and second transceiver instance (sheet instance refs U20/C29-C32/R36 vs board region near U1) could not be fully inspected; full net list for CAN2 node count is unverified.\",\"ERC and netlist checks were malformed (missing sheet file), so no machine electrical-rules coverage exists for any sheet; my connectivity review covers only the supplied wbo-can-trans sheet.\",\"Root schematic and all other sheets (including VR conditioner) were not supplied; parent-side wiring of the CAN2+/CAN2- hierarchical pins and whether CAN2 is exposed on the external harness could not be confirmed.\",\"No CAN bit rate, bus length, or termination requirement is stated in the packet, so the DNP-termination finding is bounded to a concern.\",\"No component datasheet data beyond symbol fields was available; part ratings (e.g., NUP2105L 24Vrwm vs automotive transients) were not assessed per declared scope.\",\"Saved copper evaluated as-is; zone refill forbidden per candidate constraints.\"],\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"F1-sheet-file-case-mismatch\",\"title\":\"Hierarchy references 'VR Conditioner.kicad_sch' but checkout supplies 'VR conditioner.kicad_sch'; ERC and netlist coverage lost\",\"location\":\"project root sheet reference -> VR Conditioner.kicad_sch (checkout: VR conditioner.kicad_sch)\",\"condition\":\"Any case-sensitive filesystem (as used by the native toolchain here) loading the project hierarchy.\",\"mechanism\":\"The sheet file reference fails to resolve, so eeschema cannot build the full hierarchy: ERC and netlist generation abort (both checks executed 'malformed'), and DRC schematic parity flags all 15 VR-conditioner board components (U10 MAX9924, R25-R34, C23-C25, JP1) as 'Extra footprint' because they exist on the board but not in the loaded schematic. All electrical rule verification for the entire project is therefore unestablished.\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"assessment\":\"defect\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/drc/drc.json\",\"locator\":\"schematic_parity entries type=extra_footprint for C25 (uuid 0070999b), R28 (40773cef), U10 (4ccdf03c), R27 (4f184bcb), R29 (667488c6), R32, C24, R33, R30, R25, JP1, R26, C23, R31, R34\"},{\"path\":\"work/geometry/geometry.json\",\"locator\":\"footprint ref U10 value MAX9924 with live nets (/VR1+, Net-(U10-IN+), +5V) and footprints R27/R28/R29 on Net-(U10-IN+/-): components wired on the board yet absent from the loaded schematic\"},{\"path\":\"work/drc/console.log\",\"locator\":\"line 3: 'Found 114 schematic parity issues'\"}],\"reasoning\":\"The ERC and netlist checks both report missing_sheet_files=['VR Conditioner.kicad_sch'] and the declared limitation confirms the checkout filename is lower-case 'conditioner'. The parity extra_footprint set is exactly the VR-conditioner analog front end (MAX9924 plus its bias/filter network), which proves the board implements a sheet the schematic hierarchy cannot load. This is a native violation of project integrity, not a tool failure, and it blocks all machine electrical verification of the design as supplied.\"},{\"id\":\"F2-drc-error-violations\",\"title\":\"Native DRC reports 13 error-severity violations: 5 padstack, 5 annular_width, 3 starved_thermal\",\"location\":\"inputs/project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb (saved board, sha256 4e059d57...)\",\"condition\":\"Board fabricated/assembled as saved; zones evaluated as saved per read-only constraint.\",\"mechanism\":\"Annular-width and padstack errors indicate pad/via geometry below the board's own constraints, risking drill breakout and unreliable plated connections; starved thermal errors indicate zone thermal-relief spokes insufficient for the connected pads, risking poor solder joints or an effectively open zone connection.\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"assessment\":\"defect\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/drc/console.log\",\"locator\":\"line 1: 'Found 142 violations' (kicad-cli pcb drc --severity-all, exit 0)\"},{\"path\":\"work/drc/drc.json\",\"locator\":\"violations[] (error-severity items lie beyond the included 100000-byte prefix; check summary by_severity error=13, by_type padstack=5, annular_width=5, starved_thermal=3)\"},{\"path\":\"work/drc/execution.json\",\"locator\":\"argv kicad-cli pcb drc --format json --severity-all --schematic-parity; exit_code 0\"}],\"reasoning\":\"The DRC run executed cleanly against the exact board sha and natively reported 13 violations at error severity whose types (padstack, annular width, starved thermal) are manufacturing/reliability defects rather than cosmetic warnings. A zero exit code does not clear these; they are real rule violations in the saved copper. The specific items are truncated from the supplied artifact prefix, so affected references should be confirmed from the full drc.json, but the counts and types are tool-reported facts.\"},{\"id\":\"F3-can2-termination-dnp\",\"title\":\"Both internal CAN2 (wideband bus) 120R terminations are DNP; bus has no populated termination\",\"location\":\"inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch R36 (instances R36/R37) across /CAN2+ and /CAN2-\",\"condition\":\"Operating the internal wideband CAN bus (ECU brain CAN2 transceiver U21 plus wideband module transceivers) without user-added external termination.\",\"mechanism\":\"With both 120R resistors unpopulated, differential termination is only the transceivers' internal bias (tens of kilohms). Recessive-state transitions must discharge the bus capacitance (including the four populated 47p filter caps C29/C30/C33/C34 plus trace and transceiver capacitance) through that high impedance, giving microsecond-scale edges that corrupt bits at typical CAN rates; reflections are also undamped. Internal wideband communication would be unreliable or nonfunctional unless termination exists elsewhere.\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"assessment\":\"concern\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch\",\"locator\":\"symbol uuid d69380f9-5487-4782-9ce9-0690df62e543: R36 value 120, (dnp yes), (in_bom no); text 'n.p.' uuid 98ed307b at (113.03 76.2); wiring ties R36 pins to CAN2+ (y=83.82) and CAN2- (y=88.9)\"},{\"path\":\"work/geometry/geometry.json\",\"locator\":\"dnp_refs includes R36 and R37; footprint R36 (uuid starting ed50429c pad entries) dnp=true with pad1 net /CAN2+ and pad2 net /CAN2- at ~(175.0, 142.1)\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/project/README.md\",\"locator\":\"'Dual wideband O2 sensor controllers ... (connected internally to CAN bus #2)'\"}],\"reasoning\":\"The DNP is clearly intentional (schematic 'n.p.' note), which suggests the designers expect termination elsewhere, possibly external on the harness since /CAN2+ also appears on module-connector pads (J2 pad 73 per DRC items). But the packet contains no evidence of any populated termination anywhere on CAN2, and the README presents the wideband link as internal. If the bus is used as documented with no external nodes, it is unterminated and likely nonfunctional. Because the intended system-level termination strategy is unstated and the root schematic is unavailable, this is reported as a concern rather than a defect, but it directly challenges the packet's stated scope of internal dual-wideband CAN termination.\"},{\"id\":\"F4-footprint-library-hygiene\",\"title\":\"J2 brain-module footprint differs from symbol-specified footprint and 'Simon' footprint library is absent from configuration\",\"location\":\"Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb footprints J2, P1, P3, P5, P6, J1, J4 (library 'Simon')\",\"condition\":\"Rebuilding, re-annotating, or re-importing netlist changes on any machine without the private 'Simon' library.\",\"mechanism\":\"J2 uses Simon:Polygonus-With-USB-SWD while the symbol specifies fome_modules:polygonus; the 'Simon' library is not in the configuration, so footprint updates from library would fail or silently substitute, and 106 lib_footprint_mismatch warnings show board copies have diverged from their libraries. Risk is to interface geometry fidelity (the brain-module connector pin field) if footprints are ever refreshed.\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"assessment\":\"concern\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/drc/drc.json\",\"locator\":\"schematic_parity item: 'Simon:Polygonus-With-USB-SWD doesn't match footprint given by symbol (fome_modules:polygonus)' for Footprint J2 uuid f447e585\"},{\"path\":\"work/drc/drc.json\",\"locator\":\"violations type=lib_footprint_issues: 'The current configuration does not include the footprint library Simon' (P1 uuid 1646febd, P3, P5, P6, J1, J4)\"}],\"reasoning\":\"As saved, the board geometry is self-contained and DRC shows 0 unconnected items, so there is no demonstrated electrical fault. However, a deliberate footprint substitution on the central 112-pad module interface that contradicts the symbol field, combined with an unavailable source library, is a maintainability and reproducibility risk worth tracking; it also inflates parity noise (96 Datasheet-field mismatches, 106 library mismatches) that can mask real parity defects.\"},{\"id\":\"F5-canrx-label-direction\",\"title\":\"Hierarchical label CAN_RX declared shape 'input' but is driven by transceiver RXD output\",\"location\":\"inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch hierarchical_label CAN_RX at (204.47, 83.82)\",\"condition\":\"ERC review of the sheet (currently impossible because ERC is malformed per F1).\",\"mechanism\":\"The label connects to U20/U21 pin 4 (RXD, declared output). Declaring the sheet port as input misstates signal direction; electrically the net still forms, but ERC pin-conflict checking at the parent sheet pin is weakened and future edits may wire a driver against RXD.\",\"severity\":\"info\",\"assessment\":\"concern\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch\",\"locator\":\"hierarchical_label 'CAN_RX' (shape input) uuid 0cfcbd19; wire uuid 327ec337 (179.07,83.82)-(204.47,83.82) to U20 RXD pin 4 (output, at mirrored position 179.07,83.82)\"}],\"reasoning\":\"No functional impact in the current wiring (RXD correctly drives the port toward the parent), and CAN_TX ('input' driving TXD) is correct. This is a documentation/ERC-hygiene nit; it matters mainly because ERC cannot currently run (F1) to police such direction mismatches project-wide.\"}]}","structured_output":{"schema":"agent-ee.review/1","candidate_id":"693f8163ce687e039a86a686decde90440b8c14b5ae3b38c294486b2f1e4fb44","run_id":"c6cb3775-cb6c-446f-acaa-f3eb7229b643","packet_sha256":"2f16df3dacf72f02af6230e7ed9761372c19b736602edfe3e470ab96942af3c2","role":"circuit","coverage":["Traced inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch net-by-net: TJA1051T-3 pinout (TXD pin1->CAN_TX, RXD pin4->CAN_RX, VCC pin3->+5V with C31 100n, VIO pin5->+3.3V with C32 100n, S pin8->GND normal mode, GND pin2->GND, CANH pin7->CAN2+, CANL pin6->CAN2-); no CANH/CANL swap found under y-mirror transform.","Verified NUP2105L dual ESD clamp (D10/D11) cathodes to CAN2+ and CAN2-, anode pin3 to GND; verified 47p filter caps C29/C30 from CAN2+/CAN2- to GND in both sheet instances.","Checked internal dual-wideband CAN2 termination: sheet resistor R36 (120R, 1206) is dnp/in_bom-no with 'n.p.' annotation; confirmed on saved board that both instance refs R36 and R37 bridge /CAN2+ to /CAN2- and appear in geometry dnp_refs.","Cross-checked board geometry pad nets for U21 (TJA1051T-3: /CAN_TX2, /CAN_RX2, /CAN2+, /CAN2-, +5V, +3.3V, GND) and U1 (f042_wideband_module: /CAN_RX, /CAN_TX, /LSU_* pins) within the included geometry prefix.","Reviewed DRC execution record (kicad-cli 10.0.7, exit 0, severity-all with schematic parity), console log counts (142 violations, 0 unconnected, 114 parity issues), and the included prefix of work/drc/drc.json (parity warnings, silk_over_copper, lib_footprint_mismatch/issues, extra_footprint list).","Correlated the 15 extra_footprint parity items (U10 MAX9924, R25-R34, C23-C25, JP1) with the missing 'VR Conditioner.kicad_sch' sheet file that caused ERC and netlist checks to be malformed.","Confirmed DRC reports zero unconnected items on the saved board (fill state as saved).","Sa